//  M.A.U.S. UTILITY UNIT -- AMPHIBIOUS PLACEHOLDER BODY VARIANT
//
//  Sibling of the drone, flyer and aquatic monsterparts. Read the drone's for
//  how category + type binding works; only what DIFFERS is recorded here.
//
//  Own category, therefore own monsterpart, therefore own pngs -- the engine
//  picks at random from every monsterpart matching a category, so a shared one
//  would have the four chassis wearing each other's bodies.
//
//  HUE-SPACE IS EXHAUSTED AT FOUR CHASSIS, AND THIS IS WHERE IT RAN OUT.
//
//  The other three were chosen by simulating deuteranopia and protanopia
//  (Vienot 1999) and comparing tier by tier -- brightest against brightest --
//  because all four sprites share identical structure, so the comparison a
//  player actually makes is the same pixel on two units. Worst-case luminance
//  separation, x100:
//
//      drone pink    vs flyer blue      1.9   <- already weak
//      aquatic green vs drone pink      9.2
//      aquatic green vs flyer blue     11.8
//      amphibious purple vs drone pink  0.4   <- this one
//      amphibious purple vs flyer blue  0.9
//      amphibious purple vs aquatic    10.7
//
//  Purple sits BETWEEN pink and blue in hue, so under red-green colour
//  blindness it collapses against both. Every value and saturation variant was
//  searched; the best available was 3.6 and only by darkening it to 0.35 value,
//  which stops a FULLBRIGHT GLOW LAYER reading as a glow at all. Not worth
//  trading the thing's whole purpose for two points of separation.
//
//  SO THE FINDING IS RECORDED RATHER THAN THE PROBLEM SOLVED: a fifth chassis
//  cannot be told apart by hue, and neither can this one from the drone under
//  colour blindness. The answer when real art lands is SHAPE or a marking --
//  a fin, a rotor, a plate -- not another colour. Green worked because it is
//  naturally the brightest at equal saturation; there is no second slot like
//  that left.

{
  "name" : "amphibious_placeholder",
  "category" : "petports_amphibious",
  "type" : "body",

  "frames" : {
    "body" : "body_0_lit.png",
    "bodyfullbright" : "body_0_fullbright.png"
  }
}
